::::box{as=section class="chapter reveal" #why}

::::box{class=eyebrow}
The three decisions
::::

## Why it is built this way

::::box{class=lead}
Every language that extends Markdown makes the same three choices. These are ours, and each one
is held by a test rather than by intent.
::::

::::box{class=features}

:::card[Markdown first, not Markdown-shaped]{}
A document containing no HyMarkX construct renders as CommonMark plus GFM, byte for byte. That
is not a goal, it is a gate: 692 conformance examples run on every commit, and a regression
fails the build rather than becoming a footnote.
:::

:::card[The output is proportional]{}
A document that uses no component emits no component CSS. One with no interactive construct
emits no JavaScript at all — not a smaller runtime, none.
:::

:::card[Safe by default, not by discipline]{}
Trust mode is chosen by the host, and nothing inside a document can raise it. Expressions cannot
reach the network, storage, timers or any host object — which is why the copy buttons on this
page are host code rather than something the document was able to ask for.
:::

::::

::::box{class=figure}
![How HyMarkX compiles a document: the document is parsed into an AST where every node carries a source span, then compiled. HTML is always emitted, CSS only when the document is styled, and JavaScript is zero bytes unless the document uses an interactive construct.](/pipeline.svg)
::::

::::

