::::box{as=section class="chapter reveal" #start}

::::box{class=eyebrow}
Two commands
::::

## Start

::::box{class=lead}
Point it at a Markdown file you already have. Nothing in that file has to change for it to
compile.
::::

```sh
npm install hymarkx
```

```sh
npx hmx build index.md --out dist
```

::::box{class=start}

:::note[Also in the box]{type=info}
`hmx check` for CI, `hmx fmt` that leaves your prose alone, and `hmx dev` with live reload.
There is a [VS Code extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=name0x0.hymarkx)
with a real language server behind it — diagnostics, completion, hover and formatting.
:::

